title The corpus was never the cost, the loop around it was
prompt kg -- take the roster-cost lap
think The obvious move was the wrong one and I nearly took it. My own recommendation last turn was to move the five slowest guards to tier cadence, and the numbers that justified it -- top five holding 46 percent of 1,510 seconds -- are the same numbers that should have raised a question first. A 137-second ASCII check over nine small files is not slow, it is broken. Reading the script rather than reaching for the tier is what found the fault.
think living_card_ascii validated UTF-8 by calling a shell function once per file across 14,709 tracked text files, and that function forked mktemp, iconv and rm every time. Roughly 44,000 processes for a reading the bytes make trivial. The corpus was never the cost.
think reds_row_present was the same shape one layer up: the witness asked the script for row 1, then row 2, to the end of the ledger -- 411 invocations, each re-reading the pin plus forty archives. Same lesson, different room.
obs Before you make an expensive thing rare, find out whether it is expensive on purpose. A cadence tier applied to those two would have hidden 277 seconds of pure waste behind a slower clock and left the waste sitting there, still costing on every fifth lap and now invisible.
obs The awk validator is proven both ways in a five-file pen rather than only against ASCII: clean and valid-multibyte pass, orphan lead byte and bare continuation and overlong lead refuse. A validator proven only against ASCII would have passed all three of the refusals. Then proven again on the real tree by planting an orphan lead byte and watching the guard name its path.
obs NUL-delimited on purpose. The first prototype used a whitespace-split list and git ls-files handed back a path with a space in it, which xargs tore in half and awk then failed to open. A list that drops files in silence is the reading a guard can least afford, and the fault announced itself only because awk was loud about the missing file.
obs The --all mode answers from the SAME sed expressions over the SAME spine file set, so the witness keeps that script as its authority rather than growing a second reader beside it. And the single-row path stays proven on first, middle, last and past-the-end, because a completeness leg running only --all would leave the contract seventeen scans depend on tested by nothing -- which is %410's shape exactly, met again two hours later.
obs sow is the one that moved rather than mended. Projecting the whole public seed and scrubbing every name is real work, and what makes the slower clock honest is that the act it guards is custody gate %1 -- a manual publish that runs this witness in its own flow. No lap can take the thing it protects.
obs Honest about the size of the win: 1,510s to 1,003s routine is a third, not the single digits I estimated a turn earlier when I had the shape right and no numbers. Scoped passes cut further on a small change -- 33 of 111 skipped, measured -- but the floor is the guards a lap actually touches.
loom roster before_s=1510 projected_s=1003 measured_s=990 guards_before=111 guards_after=110 median_s=2 mean_s=13
obs The projection was 1,003s and the pass measured 990 -- within 1.3 percent, which is what a per-guard cost card buys over a guess. 110 guards rather than 111 because sow now answers on the cadence clock. run_verdict=ok, 106 green, zero red, four gated.
obs That measurement landed after the hot pass had already opened, so the pass read a tree differing from the commit by this log's own two lines. Named rather than glossed, as the shell_dialect repair was: no guard reads a session log's body, and re-running twenty-seven minutes to reprove 110 unchanged readings would cost more than the honesty is worth.
loom guard=living_card_ascii before_s=137 after_s=25 files=14709 forks_before=44127
loom guard=reds_row_present before_s=177 after_s=12 invocations_before=411 invocations_after=1
file tools/fixtures/l/utf8_valid.awk one process for the whole corpus, LC_ALL=C so substr counts bytes, three malformed shapes refused by name
file tools/fixtures/l/living_card_ascii_scan.sh the fork loop replaced, the self-proof widened from two shapes to five
file tools/fixtures/r/reds_row_present.sh an --all mode from the same sed and the same spine, so the authority is unchanged
file tools/r/reds_row_present_witness.rish completeness in one pass, and the single-row contract still proven four ways
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri sow moved to tier cadence, with the gate that makes the slower clock honest written beside it
recommend kg -- petrichor and pheromone are two commands away and the pass they will pay is a third cheaper than it was this morning
